# A public loop off the Millrace, with a second way out through the Garden Plots.
Place foundry_court in millrace.
Name: Foundry Court
Description: The old foundry yard has become a little public square. Brick arches shelter a noticeboard, a drinking fountain, and a long table of donated timber. The workshop is north. East follows the canal; northeast returns to the Millrace. Broad level paths connect every doorway. The board explains a six-stop walk and three free projects, with supplies provided.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Smell: Warm brick, sawdust, and the cool mineral smell of canal water.
Listen: Water runs beyond the east rail. Through the workshop doorway come brushes on wood and light taps at a bench.
Doings: Open the town guide, follow the Canal trail, or start a project in the Repair Hall.
Northeast: millrace_channel
North: repair_hall
East: canal_towpath
Action: read the foundry board | Read the foundry board | The board shows how water powered the mills and how their empty buildings became shared workshops. A raised line follows the canal from the court to the garden. Your notebook records the first stop. | page | traces the canal route on the foundry noticeboard.

Place repair_hall in millrace.
Name: the Repair Hall
Description: A former machine shop has wide doors, high brick windows, and sturdy benches at different heights. Hand tools hang in labeled outlines. A tray holds pre-cut timber for a bird shelter: choose a shape, smooth the edges, then assemble it. No tools or money are needed from home. South returns to Foundry Court; southeast opens onto the towpath.
Outside: no
Ground: wood.interior
Ambience: amb.netloft.room
Smell: Cedar shavings, linseed oil, and clean cotton work aprons.
Listen: Sandpaper brushes wood. Someone taps a small joint into place across the hall.
Doings: Make a bird shelter, inspect the tools, or invite a friend to work alongside you.
South: foundry_court
Southeast: canal_towpath
Action: inspect the tool wall | Inspect the tool wall | Each tool has a raised outline and a plain label. The timber is already cut; a clamp keeps it still while you work. You learn how the benches make room for different ways of working. Your notebook records the Repair Hall. | page | explores the labeled tool wall in the Repair Hall.

Place canal_towpath in millrace.
Name: the Canal Towpath
Description: A wide brick path follows the narrow old mill channel. A continuous rail separates the walk from the water. West leads to Foundry Court, northwest to the Repair Hall, and east to the Lock Garden. Marks on the coping show how high the water used to run. Benches break the walk into easy stretches.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Water: canal
Ambience: amb.canal.water
Smell: Wet brick, river moss, and leaves drying on the path.
Listen: A steady stream slides along the wall. Water falls over a low sill farther east.
Doings: Read the water marks, sit with somebody, or follow the rail to the Lock Garden.
West: foundry_court
Northwest: repair_hall
East: lock_garden
Action: read the water marks | Read the water marks | You follow three horizontal grooves in the coping: low water, working water, and the old flood line. The middle groove led water toward the mill wheels. You add a rubbing and a written description to your notebook. | page | makes a rubbing of the canal water marks.

Place lock_garden in sweetwater.
Name: the Lock Garden
Description: The old lock is a sheltered water garden now. Water spills across a shallow stone sill into a reed bed. The lock machinery is fenced off, but a safe table holds a small working model. West returns along the towpath. North goes under the Glass Canopy; east follows a gently rising path to the overlook.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Water: canal
Ambience: amb.canal.water
Smell: Water mint, wet stone, and the muddy sweetness of reeds.
Listen: Close water spills over the sill; reed stems rattle softly beyond it.
Doings: Try the model lock, examine the reed bed, or take the level path to the Glass Canopy.
West: canal_towpath
North: glass_canopy
East: canal_overlook
Action: examine the reed bed | Examine the reed bed | A sign explains that the roots slow the water and catch sediment. You compare a rough reed stem with a smooth mint leaf at the accessible planter. The water is clearest downstream of the roots. Your notebook records what the garden does. | hangout.page | examines the reed-bed planter beside the old lock.

Place glass_canopy in sweetwater.
Name: the Glass Canopy
Description: A light iron-and-glass roof shelters potting benches around a broad, level aisle. Vents stand open above trays of seedlings. Labels can be read or traced by hand. Pots, compost, and herb cuttings are free to use here. South returns to the Lock Garden; west reaches the Garden Plots and the rest of Sweetwater Park.
Outside: no
Ground: linoleum
Ambience: amb.reeds.breeze
Smell: Damp compost, mint, and green tomato stems.
Listen: Leaves stir beneath the open vents. A watering can pours into a tray at the far bench.
Doings: Grow an herb cutting, compare the herb labels, or meet a friend at the potting table.
South: lock_garden
West: garden_plots
Action: compare the herbs | Compare the herbs | Mint has a cool scent and a square stem. Rosemary is resinous, with narrow firm leaves. Lemon balm smells of citrus when a leaf is gently rubbed. You write all three differences in your notebook; sight is only one way to tell them apart. | hangout.page | compares the herb labels and scents beneath the canopy.

Place canal_overlook in sweetwater.
Name: the Canal Overlook
Description: A gently sloping path ends at a broad terrace above the lock. The continuous rail meets a raised model of the canal, mills, and river. The terrace has backed benches and enough turning room beside them. West is the only way out, returning to the Lock Garden. From here the route you just walked makes sense as a whole.
Outside: yes
Ground: cobble
Water: canal
Ambience: amb.reeds.breeze
Smell: Open river air and thyme growing between the terrace stones.
Listen: Water below, leaves behind you, and the distant working hum of Millrace.
Doings: Trace the canal model, read your notebook, or rest on the terrace.
West: lock_garden
Action: trace the canal model | Trace the canal model | Your hand follows water from the river, through the lock, past the mill sites, and back downstream. The court, workshop, towpath, garden, and canopy each have a distinct marker. You record how they connect: one waterway, with a different purpose at every stop. | page | traces the raised canal model at the overlook.

Link millrace_channel southwest to foundry_court.
Link garden_plots east to glass_canopy.
